Carafe: while the runtime asks for them, a flush of a shown window is reported with wine_nx_screen_picture_drawn
(patch 0106) when the program itself drew into the surface since the last flush (wine_nx_driver_surface_drawn,
patches 0112 and 0114) and its client area holds something other than black, together with the window's thread and
whether the flush draws over pixels already on the screen with others (wine_nx_layer_redrawn, patch 0115). The
frame, the caption and the background fill are the system's (patch 0113).
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

